change based on your queries.  \\r\\n- **Remember to flush the output buffer** after each write; otherwise, you may receive a **Time Limit Exceeded** verdict.  \\r\\n  - In C: `fflush(stdout);`  \\r\\n  - In C++: `cout.flush();`  \\r\\n  - In Python: `sys.stdout.flush()`  \\r\\n  - In Java: `System.out.flush();`  \\r\\n  - In Kotlin: `System.out.flush()`\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n**Input Description:**  \\r\\n- A single integer ~N~ (~1 \\\\leq N \\\\leq 10^5~), the upper bound for the coordinates.  \\r\\n- The interactor responses to your queries in the described format.\\r\\n\\r\\n**Output Description:**  \\r\\n- Your questions in the format `? x y`.  \\r\\n- Finally, the coordinates of the treasure in the format `r c`.\\r\\n\\r\\n---\\r\\n\\r\\n**Test Cases:**\\r\\n\\r\\n**Test Case 1:** *(Simulated interaction example)*\\r\\n\\r\\n<table>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<th>Input (Interactor)</th>\\r\\n<th>Output (Program)</th>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<pre>\\r\\n10\\r\\n? 0 0\\r\\n14\\r\\n? 7 7\\r\\n4\\r\\n? 9 5\\r\\n0\\r\\n</pre>\\r\\n</td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<pre>\\r\\n9 5\\r\\n</pre>\\r\\n</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n</table>\\r\\n\\r\\n\\r\\n**Test Cases:**\\r\\n\\r\\n**Test Case 1:** *(Simulated interaction example)*\\r\\n\\r\\n<table>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<th>Input (Interactor)</th>\\r\\n<th>Output (Program)</th>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n<tr>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<pre>\\r\\n10\\r\\n? 0 0\\r\\n14\\r\\n? 7 7\\r\\n4\\r\\n? 9 5\\r\\n0\\r\\n</pre>\\r\\n</td>\\r\\n<td>\\r\\n<pre>\\r\\n9 5\\r\\n</pre>\\r\\n</td>\\r\\n</tr>\\r\\n</table>\", \"group\": 2, \"time_limit\": 1.0, \"memory_limit\": 102400, \"short_circuit\": false, \"points\": 1.0, \"partial\": false, \"is_public\": false, \"is_manually_managed\": false, \"date\": \"2025-11-08T15:47:07-05:00\", \"license\": null, \"og_image\": \"\", \"summary\": \"\", \"user_count\": 0, \"ac_rate\": 0.0, \"is_full_markup\": false, \"submission_source_visibility_mode\": \"F\", \"is_organization_private\": true, \"authors\": [2], \"curators\": [2], \"testers\